afk: yield accepts whole-array payloads for array-valued sections.

The yield tool's parameter schema (withSectionVariants) advertises the
whole array branch for array-valued sections like `findings`, but the
per-section validator only accepted a single element and assembly nested
a submitted array one level deep — every reviewer that batched findings
burned schema-retry round trips. Array payloads for array-valued
sections now validate against the property schema and splat into the
section; the tool description says so.

What must survive a rebase:
- output-schema-validator.ts: the per-section validator for an
  array-typed property accepts the full array (validated against the
  property schema) as well as one element.
- The section assembler splats an array payload for array-valued labels
  instead of nesting it. Since 18.2.x that assembler lives in
  packages/tui/src/tools/task-yield-assembly.ts (appendYieldSection);
  coding-agent's task/yield-assembly.ts only computes arrayValuedLabels.
- Regression test in test/tools/yield.test.ts (whole-array accept,
  invalid element still rejected per call, splat + append on assembly).

